35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The minutes show the joint clinic failed because neither department owned the rota. We must avoid that trap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The readmission data is clear. The call-back trial cut returns by a fifth. It works, but only while staffed.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The midwifery rota has slack. The therapy team is bleeding staff. I see a clear imbalance in capacity.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,The ledger is thin. Off-site work earns nothing. We must build on-site to keep the tariffs.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The car park is full by eleven. The shuttle misses most villages. The booking system only holds named slots.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, the call-back trial proves the model works. But who holds the budget line this time?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,The data shows the benefit is real. The risk is the staffing gap. We need a dedicated line.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,The midwifery slack is a resource. The therapy deficit is a warning. We should not add to the deficit.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"The tariff loss is the killer. If we go off-site, we lose the revenue. We must stay on-site.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"The booking system cannot hold unstructured work. If the program needs flexible visits, it will vanish from the records.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I am worried about the agreement. If the midwifery team is the only one with slack, they will burn out.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. The readmission drop is significant. But it requires consistent, dedicated staff. Not a shared, fragile rota.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"The midwifery slack is real, but it is temporary. The therapy deficit is structural. We must not ignore the structural gap.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,The financial gap is structural. The tariff loss is immediate. We must choose a program that generates revenue on-site.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,The physical gap is immediate. The car park is full. The shuttle is missing. The booking system is rigid.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"We need a program that is self-contained. Not one that relies on a fragile, shared agreement.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,The call-back trial is self-contained. It has a clear start and end. It has a clear measure of success.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,The midwifery slack is a temporary resource. The therapy deficit is a structural problem. We must not add to the structural problem.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,The on-site requirement is non-negotiable. The tariff loss is too high. We must build on-site to keep the revenue.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,The physical capacity is the limit. The car park is full. The shuttle is missing. The booking system is rigid.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
